    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commĭnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				threatening</i>, <i>menacing</i> (rare, but in
			good prose): orationis tamquam armorum, * <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 54, 206</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				1, 33</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">taurorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 45, 70, § 181</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 26, 7, 7, §
			7</span></i>.—In plur.: imperiosae, Tiro ap.
				<i><span class="en">Gell.
				7, 3, 13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hannibalis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 8, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tiberii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 37</span></i>
			.</div>
